{
 "_doc": "#1926 THE DECLARATION of Cloud C3 > Ops > Mail > Tables, Topology-Inbound and Topology-Outbound. `tables`: each section with its columns (key = the field of a row served by cloudy-c3-api GET /mail/stack tables.<id>, or of the declared source named in `source`) and the filter columns offered; a key the API does not serve prints as 'not served', never as a blank. `topologies`: the graph (nodes with x/y in a world grid, edges with a direction from->to) and the PROBE BINDINGS: every node and edge lists probe ids served in /mail/stack probes[]; its colour is the worst served state (grey when none is served). One generic canvas (MailTopologyCanvas) renders any topology of this file; names of hosts live here and in the API, never in Kotlin. Edit this file by hand: MailStackTest pins the tables, the node and edge parity and the probe bindings. #1955 B the old Mail subpage (ops_maps.json maps.mail) is merged in: map_inbound, map_outbound and map_containers come first (source declared, map + section), Hosts, Relays + MX and DNS were already hosts_declared, relays_declared and dns_declared.",
